==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|Hyekʷ}}
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|hēpatītis}}, from {{m|la|hēpar||liver}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|ἧπαρ||liver}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˌhɛpəˈtaɪ̯tɪs/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-hepatitis.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|hepatitises|hepatitides}}

# [[inflammation|Inflammation]] of the [[liver]], sometimes caused by a [[viral]] [[infection]].
#* '''2013''', Teri Shors, ''Understanding Viruses'', 2nd edition
#*: '''Hepatitises''' B and C are the most important chronic viral infections of humans.

